---
// /brands/la-cornue-range-repair/ — Luxury Wave L-3. La Cornue (France, founded 1908).
// WEDGE = Château (bespoke, France-built, vaulted oven, special-order France parts, long
// lead) vs CornuFé (semi-custom, conventional convection ovens, easier parts) — no
// competitor makes this distinction. Ranges & ovens ONLY (NO La Cornue refrigeration).
// NO sourced failure pattern — wear/calibration + brass/enamel restoration. Owner-neutral
// (Middleby 2015 -> 26North JV Dec 2025 = stale; not stated). $89 residential. Verified:
// La Cornue USA + Wikipedia + Yale + Coast Appliance Parts.
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ServiceHero from '../../components/ServiceHero.astro';
import BrandBranchesGrid from '../../components/BrandBranchesGrid.astro';
import { MAIN_PHONE, MAIN_PHONE_TEL } from '../../data/branches';
import { mergeCredentials } from '../../data/credentials-schema';
import { BRANCH_LOCATIONS_GEO_NEUTRAL } from '../../lib/build-location-array';
import { OPENING_HOURS_SCHEMA } from '../../data/business-hours';

const title = "La Cornue Range Repair Los Angeles — Same Day";
const description = "La Cornue Château and CornuFé range repair across Los Angeles and the Westside. The Château-vs-CornuFé difference decides parts and lead time. $89 diagnostic.";
const canonical = "https://samedayappliance.repair/brands/la-cornue-range-repair/";

const faqs = [
  { q: "What's the difference between a La Cornue Château and a CornuFé, and why does it matter for repair?", a: "It's the single most important thing to know before anyone services your La Cornue, and most repair pages skip it. The Château is the bespoke, hand-built La Cornue — the iconic vaulted 'voûte' oven, brass trim, custom configuration, built in France. Its most specialized parts are special-order from France, which means longer lead times on certain components. The CornuFé (the CornuFé 90 and CornuFé 110, sold through retailers like Williams-Sonoma and AJ Madison) is the semi-custom, more accessible line — it uses more conventional convection ovens and standard construction, so its parts source faster and repairs are more straightforward. When you call, tell us whether you have a Château or a CornuFé; the diagnosis is similar but the parts path and timeline are genuinely different. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair." },
  { q: "Does La Cornue make refrigerators — can you fix a La Cornue fridge?", a: "La Cornue makes ranges and ovens, plus matching hoods — not refrigeration. If you've seen a page advertising 'La Cornue refrigerator repair,' that's a service padding its brand list, because there isn't a La Cornue fridge to repair. What La Cornue builds is the range: the Château, the CornuFé, and the CornuChef, all cooking appliances. We service those. If your kitchen pairs a La Cornue range with a Sub-Zero or a separate luxury fridge, we cover those too — just under the correct brand." },
  { q: "How long do La Cornue parts take to get in LA?", a: "It depends entirely on Château versus CornuFé. For a CornuFé, the more conventional construction means many parts source through domestic channels in a normal timeframe. For a Château, the specialized and bespoke components can be special-order from France, and those carry real lead time — sometimes weeks. La Cornue USA runs a servicer network and a national service center, and California OEM parts are also carried through channels like Coast Appliance Parts, so the common wear items are obtainable here. Our techs will tell you honestly, part by part, whether something is on hand, domestic, or a France order — no surprises on the timeline. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair." },
  { q: "My La Cornue oven isn't reaching temperature — what's the fix?", a: "On the Château's vaulted oven and on the CornuFé's convection oven, an oven that won't reach or hold temperature usually comes down to the heating element or burner, the thermostat or temperature sensor, and calibration. Our techs put a calibrated thermometer in the cavity, check the actual versus set temperature across the range, and test the element or gas burner and the thermostat. On a gas Château we also check the safety valve and thermocouple. It's rarely a mystery — it's a heat-source, sensor, or calibration issue, and on a range at this level it's virtually always worth the repair." },
  { q: "Can you restore the brass and enamel on an older La Cornue?", a: "The brass trim and enameled surfaces are a big part of why people own a La Cornue, and they're serviceable. Worn or tarnished brass fittings and knobs, and chipped or crazed enamel, are cosmetic-and-mechanical work we can address as part of a service — sourcing genuine trim through the La Cornue channel where a piece needs replacing rather than restoring. On a Château especially, keeping the brass and enamel right is part of maintaining the range's value, so it's worth doing properly with correct parts rather than generic substitutes." },
  { q: "Is a La Cornue always worth repairing?", a: "Yes. A CornuFé is a $12,000-to-$18,000 range and a Château runs from roughly $35,000 well past $100,000 — these are heirloom appliances and the centerpiece of the kitchen in a Beverly Hills or Bel Air estate. Even a significant repair, including a Château part on a France order, is a fraction of replacement, and the range holds its value. There's essentially no scenario where a La Cornue is 'totaled' by a repair. We'll give you the honest number and the honest timeline, but the answer on a La Cornue is repair." },
  { q: "How fast can you reach a La Cornue on the Westside?", a: "Same-day in most cases across Los Angeles, Beverly Hills, Bel Air, Malibu, and the Westside, with our other branches covering Orange County, Ventura, San Bernardino, and Riverside. La Cornue ranges cluster in the estate belt, which is our densest area, so a Château or CornuFé call in Beverly Hills or the Palisades is usually a fast response. We answer 24/7. The one honest caveat is Château parts lead time — the visit is fast, but a France-order part can extend the full repair, and we'll tell you that up front. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair." }
];

const schema = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@graph": [
  { "@type": "Service", "serviceType": "La Cornue Range Repair", "provider": { "@id": canonical + "#org" }, "areaServed": [
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Los Angeles County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Orange County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Ventura County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Santa Barbara County" }, { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "San Bernardino County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Riverside County" }, { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "San Diego County" }
    ], "description": "La Cornue range repair across Los Angeles and the Westside. Château (bespoke vaulted oven) and CornuFé (semi-custom) ranges and ovens — heating elements, gas burners, thermostats, calibration, brass and enamel restoration. Château-versus-CornuFé parts-path distinction. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair." },
  { "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": faqs.map(f => ({ "@type": "Question", "name": f.q, "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": f.a.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, '') } })) },
  { "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [ { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://samedayappliance.repair/" }, { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Brands", "item": "https://samedayappliance.repair/brands/" }, { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "La Cornue Range Repair", "item": canonical } ] }
] };

const wave46OrgSchema = mergeCredentials({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'HomeAndConstructionBusiness',
  '@id': canonical + '#org',
  name: 'Same Day Appliance Repair',
  url: canonical,
  priceRange: '$$',
  openingHoursSpecification: OPENING_HOURS_SCHEMA,
  areaServed: [
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Los Angeles County' },
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Orange County' },
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Ventura County' },
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Santa Barbara County' }, { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'San Bernardino County' },
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Riverside County' }, { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'San Diego County' }
  ],
  location: BRANCH_LOCATIONS_GEO_NEUTRAL
});
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical}>
  <Fragment slot="head-scripts">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(wave46OrgSchema)} />
  </Fragment>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
  <div class="call-banner"><div class="wrap"><span>La Cornue needs service? Same-day on the Westside:</span><a href={`tel:${MAIN_PHONE_TEL}`} class="phone-lg">{MAIN_PHONE}</a></div></div>
  <ServiceHero
    section="brands"
    slug="la-cornue-range-repair"
    eyebrow={"La Cornue Range Repair"}
    title={"La Cornue Range Repair, Los Angeles & the Westside"}
    subtitle={description}
    heroImageTitle={"La Cornue Château & CornuFé Range Repair"}
  />

  <BrandBranchesGrid />
  <section class="trust-bar"><div class="wrap"><span>Licensed BHGS #A49573 · Insured</span><span>Same-day · 7 Southern California counties</span><span>$89 residential diagnostic · waived with repair</span></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>La Cornue — and why Château vs. CornuFé decides the repair</h2>
    <p>La Cornue has built ranges in France since 1908, and it's the range you find at the heart of the most serious estate kitchens in Beverly Hills, Bel Air, and Malibu. But "La Cornue repair" isn't one thing, and the first job on any service call is knowing which La Cornue you own — because the Château and the CornuFé are genuinely different machines to fix. The Château is the bespoke, hand-built range with the iconic vaulted "voûte" oven and brass trim, built to order in France, and its most specialized parts are special-order from France with real lead time. The CornuFé — the CornuFé 90 and 110 — is the semi-custom line with more conventional convection ovens and standard construction, so its parts source faster and its repairs are more straightforward. Same brand, same diagnostic care, very different parts path. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair, BHGS #A49573, EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410).</p>
    <p>Most La Cornue repair pages you'll find never make that distinction — they run one generic template and quote a timeline they can't keep. Our techs start the other way around: Château or CornuFé, gas or dual-fuel, which oven, and then we tell you honestly what's on hand, what's a domestic order, and what has to come from France. That's the difference between a promise and a plan.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap">
    <h2>La Cornue models we service</h2>
    <div class="model-grid">
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Château (75 / 90 / 120 / 150)</h3><p>The bespoke flagship — vaulted "voûte" oven, brass trim, built to order in France, sized by width. Service: gas burners and safety valves, the vaulted oven's heat source and thermostat, calibration, brass and enamel. Specialized parts can be a France special-order — we set the timeline honestly.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>CornuFé 90 & CornuFé 110</h3><p>The semi-custom La Cornue with conventional convection ovens and standard construction — the more serviceable line, with faster-sourcing parts. Common in LA kitchens that want the La Cornue look without the full Château lead time.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>CornuChef</h3><p>La Cornue's cooking line beyond the Château and CornuFé — serviced on the same gas-and-oven principles: burners, valves, oven heat source, thermostat, calibration.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Brass &amp; enamel restoration</h3><p>Tarnished brass trim and knobs, chipped or crazed enamel — cosmetic-and-mechanical service that keeps a Château's value, using genuine La Cornue trim where a piece needs replacing.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Matching La Cornue hoods</h3><p>The ventilation La Cornue offers to match the range — fan motor, switch, and lighting service. See also our <a href="/brands/la-cornue-range-hood-repair/">La Cornue range hood repair</a> page.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Gas &amp; dual-fuel diagnostics</h3><p>Burner ignition, weak flame, an oven that won't reach temperature — the gas-side and heat-source diagnosis that covers both Château and CornuFé.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>Getting La Cornue parts in LA</h2>
    <p>The parts story splits the same way the models do. For a CornuFé, the conventional construction means many components source domestically in a normal timeframe — an oven element, a thermostat, a burner part is usually a matter of days. For a Château, the bespoke and specialized components can be special-order from France, and those carry genuine lead time. La Cornue USA runs a servicer network and a national service center, and California OEM parts are carried through channels like Coast Appliance Parts, so the everyday wear items are obtainable in Los Angeles either way.</p>
    <p>What our techs do differently is tell you which bucket each part falls in before you commit — on hand, domestic order, or France. On a Château, that honesty about lead time is the whole game: the diagnostic visit is fast, but if the fix needs a France-order part, you should know that on day one, not week three. We'll keep the common wear items moving quickly and be straight with you about the specialized ones.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>What La Cornue service costs</h2>
    <p>$89 flat residential diagnostic, waived with repair. Typical service ranges (Château specialized parts can shift a line, and a France-order part carries lead time):</p>
    <table class="price-table"><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Typical range (parts + labor)</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Oven thermostat recalibration</td><td>$150–$280</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Thermocouple / safety valve (gas)</td><td>$220–$420</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Burner igniter / spark module</td><td>$220–$420</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Oven element or thermostat replacement</td><td>$280–$540</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Gas valve replacement</td><td>$320–$600</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Brass / enamel trim service</td><td>$240–$600+</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Château specialized part (France order)</td><td>quoted per part + lead time</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <p class="small">Ranges are typical; the CornuFé generally sources faster and cheaper than an equivalent Château part. We quote Château France-order parts individually with the lead time stated up front.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>Related luxury range pages</h2>
    <ul class="related-links">
      <li><a href="/brands/lacanche-range-repair/">Lacanche range repair Los Angeles</a> — the all-analog French range</li>
      <li><a href="/brands/officine-gullo-range-repair/">Officine Gullo range repair Los Angeles</a> — hand-built Florentine ranges</li>
      <li><a href="/brands/la-cornue/">La Cornue brand hub</a> — Château vs CornuFé, why these ranges have no error codes, parts and the factory channel</li>
      <li><a href="/brands/la-cornue-range-hood-repair/">La Cornue range hood repair Los Angeles</a></li>
      <li><a href="/brands/wolf-range-repair/">Wolf range repair Los Angeles</a> — American pro-range</li>
      <li><a href="/services/oven-repair/">All oven &amp; range repair in Los Angeles →</a></li>
      <li><a href="/beverly-hills/">Beverly Hills service area</a> · <a href="/malibu/">Malibu service area</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap narrow"><h2>La Cornue repair, frequently asked</h2>{faqs.map(f => <details class="faq"><summary>{f.q}</summary><p set:html={f.a}></p></details>)}</div></section>

  <section id="book" class="cta-bottom"><div class="wrap"><h2>La Cornue need service? Call the branch nearest your kitchen.</h2><p>Same-day across LA, the Westside, Orange County, Ventura, San Bernardino, and Riverside. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair.</p></div></section>
</Layout>

<style>
  body { color: var(--text); } .wrap { max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; } .wrap.narrow { max-width: 820px; }
  h1 { font-size: 2.4rem; line-height: 1.15; margin: 12px 0 20px; color: var(--black); } h2 { font-size: 1.8rem; margin: 0 0 16px; color: var(--black); } h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 0 0 10px; color: var(--black); } p { line-height: 1.65; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .call-banner { background: var(--red); color: #fff; padding: 10px 0; } .call-banner .wrap { display:flex; gap: 14px; align-items: center; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; } .call-banner .phone-lg { color:#fff; font-weight: 800; text-decoration: underline; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .trust-bar { background: var(--red); color: #fff; padding: 14px 0; } .trust-bar .wrap { display: flex; gap: 28px; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .section { padding: 56px 0; } .section.alt { background: var(--gray); }
  .model-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px; } .model-card { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 20px; border-radius: 6px; } .model-card a { color: var(--red); }
  .price-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 14px; background: #fff; } .price-table th, .price-table td { text-align: left; padding: 11px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); } .price-table th { background: var(--black); color: #fff; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.95rem; } .small { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.92rem; margin-top: 12px; }
  .related-links { list-style: none; padding: 0; } .related-links li { padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); } .related-links a { color: var(--red); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; } .related-links a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .faq { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 8px; border-radius: 4px; } .faq summary { font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; padding: 4px 0; } .faq p { margin: 8px 0 0; }
  .cta-bottom { background: var(--black); color: #fff; padding: 48px 0; } .cta-bottom h2 { color: #fff; } .cta-bottom p { color: #c9c9c9; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; } h2 { font-size: 1.45rem; }  .trust-bar .wrap { gap: 14px; font-size: 0.85rem; } }
</style>
